From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pipeline: simple: Pass the requested stride to multi-planar
 video nodes

configure() asks the video node for the stride the software ISP
prefers, but leaves the capture format's planesCount at 0.
V4L2VideoDevice::trySetFormatMultiplane() copies bytesperline only for
planesCount planes and sets num_planes from it, so a multi-planar node
never sees the request and returns its packed stride. The single-planar
path reads planes[0] unconditionally, which hid the problem there.

On the MediaTek CAMSV node (V4L2_CAP_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE), the GPU
debayer asked for 8192 bytes per 4080-pixel line, got 8160, could not
import the buffer into EGL on Panfrost and uploaded every frame on the
CPU. With the request passed through, the driver returns 8192, the
import succeeds, and the software ISP thread drops from 65% to 37% of a
core.

Set planesCount to the single plane the pipeline supports.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
index d8152ff..3beb25f 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -1636,6 +1636,7 @@ int SimplePipelineHandler::configure(Camera *camera, CameraConfiguration *c)
 	uint32_t requested_bpl = 0;
 	if (data->swIsp_)
 		requested_bpl = data->swIsp_->preferredInputStride(videoFormat.toPixelFormat(), pipeConfig->captureSize);
+	captureFormat.planesCount = 1;
 	captureFormat.planes[0].bpl = requested_bpl;
 
 	ret = video->setFormat(&captureFormat);
